# Codejitsu TODO

> Living implementation checklist. `.context/` records architectural intent; code and tests are authoritative for what is actually implemented.
>
> Updated: 2026-08-30

## Current Position

The Context Scroll / canonical resource graph slice is complete and merged into `main`. The repository now has the initial package workspace under `packages/` and the current architectural direction is recorded in `.context/architecture/`, `.context/decisions/`, `.context/current-state.ctx`, and `.context/roadmap/current.ctx`.

The old root `todo.ctx` was stale: several items described pre-graph architecture and conflicted with the current `ScrollCodex`/resource model. Those items are intentionally replaced by the checklist below rather than carried forward as zombie TODOs.

## MVP Goal

Finish Codejitsu as a small, package-oriented POC with:

- a clean package workspace/monorepo boundary
- `ScrollCodex` as the single discovery/index/resolution boundary
- source-aware URI resolution and lightweight metadata queries
- first-class resource references/graph behavior
- a complete Scroll-driven CLI
- package management exposed through Command Scrolls
- a green behavioral test suite
- no required OpenSwoole dependency
- a clean boundary so `shinobiphp/shinobi` can begin as the next repository/runtime layer

## 1. Package Workspace

Current packages present:

- [x] `packages/core`
- [x] `packages/discovery`
- [x] `packages/scrolls`
- [x] `packages/codex`
- [x] `packages/config`
- [x] `packages/schema`
- [x] `packages/console`

Remaining:

- [x] Verify each package has strict Composer metadata and the documented dependency direction.
- [ ] Map remaining root `src/` ownership explicitly before moving code.
- [ ] Move/mirror independently meaningful code into package boundaries without breaking the public `Codejitsu\\` namespace where practical.
- [x] Keep the root package as the supported development/compatibility aggregate while package source remains in root `src/`.
- [x] Verify clean Composer installation, strict PSR-4 autoloading, and real CLI bootstrap from tracked files.
- [ ] Do not create empty packages merely for symmetry; Crypto, DB, AI, OpenSwoole, and future agent concepts remain root/MVP concerns until their contracts are proven.

## 2. Codejitsu Runtime Boundary

- [x] Keep `openswoole/core` out of Codejitsu's required dependency graph.
- [ ] Remove or relocate genuinely OpenSwoole-specific runtime behavior from the Codejitsu MVP path.
- [x] Prove a clean Codejitsu install and CLI bootstrap without OpenSwoole.
- [ ] Keep long-running runtime/orchestration concerns for Shinobi.

## 3. Codex Discovery, Index & Cache

`ScrollCodex` is the single discovery/index/resolution boundary.

- [x] Make recursive resource discovery and indexing Codex-owned.
- [x] Discover registered built-in and package-owned Scroll types from configured roots.
- [x] Register project Scroll and Context discovery origins as named sources.
- [x] Maintain `IndexEntry` and discovered-resource metadata separately from hydrated Scroll instances.
- [x] Query by type, name, version, tags, attributes, source, exact/path-prefix, and references.
- [x] Preserve source provenance in indexed metadata.
- [ ] Add persistent cache/index storage.
- [ ] Validate cache freshness with a manifest/fingerprint.
- [ ] Add explicit cache rebuild/clear operations.
- [ ] Expose cache operations through Command Scrolls.
- [x] Add behavioral tests proving metadata queries do not hydrate candidates and resolution memoizes hydration.

## 4. Source-Aware URI Resolution

Logical resource identity is independent of physical source layout.

- [x] `@source` selectors are part of URI resolution, not logical identity.
- [x] Explicit source cascades are left-to-right.
- [x] Implicit resolution uses reverse registration order.
- [x] Preserve source provenance.
- [x] Verify Codex-owned source resolution with integration tests.

Examples:

```text
register @global
register @tenant

config://app
  -> @tenant -> @global

config://app@tenant.global
  -> @tenant -> @global

config://app@global.tenant
  -> @global -> @tenant
```

## 5. Resource Graph & References

- [x] Canonical Scroll representation is a semantic resource graph rather than a codec-specific array or compiler AST.
- [x] Named references normalize into graph relationships.
- [x] References are resolved lazily through the Codex.
- [ ] Make dependency/reference inspection sufficiently first-class for dependent resources to be inspected before execution.
- [x] Query indexed outgoing reference targets for the Context vertical slice.
- [ ] Preserve provenance through graph/index operations.

Example:

```text
cmd://pkg
  ├── catalog://packages
  └── capability://pkg-list
```

## 6. Context Scrolls

`.context/` is intended to become a first-class Scroll source rather than a pile of Markdown agents have to rediscover manually.

- [x] Establish `.ctx` discovery and indexing as the named `context` Codex source.
- [x] Support Markdown payloads inside Context Scrolls.
- [x] Make context queryable by logical URI, metadata, source, and relationship target.
- [x] Preserve human-readable Markdown while making metadata machine-discoverable.
- [x] Convert durable project context to `.ctx` with Git history preserved.
- [x] Prove a consumer can request targeted context by path prefix, tags, source, and reference.

## 6a. Package-Owned Scroll Types

- [x] Define immutable `TypeDefinition` metadata.
- [x] Register and look up types by name, extension, and URI scheme.
- [x] Reject name, extension, and scheme collisions.
- [x] Register built-ins while preserving the enum compatibility facade.
- [x] Support package-defined discovery, resolution, persistence, and `make:scroll` creation.
- [ ] Start `packages/ui` on a new branch and register its initial types there.

## 7. CLI / Command Scrolls

Target flow:

```text
argv
  -> CliIntent
  -> ScrollCodex
  -> Command Scroll
  -> Schema
  -> Capability
  -> execution
```

- [x] Discover and list Command Scrolls through the Codex.
- [x] Resolve commands by canonical colon-separated names.
- [x] Execute commands through the same Scroll/Codex path.
- [x] Generate namespace help/listing from stored child metadata.
- [x] Exercise `bin/codejitsu` through real subprocess smoke tests.
- [x] Cover help, listing, execution, package listing, and invalid CLI input.

## 8. Package Management

Add a minimal package-management abstraction as composition over Composer, not as a replacement dependency solver.

- [x] Create the package-management boundary only after the core package workspace is stable.
- [x] Define minimal package metadata/manifest contracts.
- [x] Implement current Composer requirement listing and package information.
- [x] Implement install/remove/update through an injectable Composer process boundary.
- [ ] Produce structured, traceable results and propagate failures cleanly.
- [x] Add network-free process-boundary fixtures for package operations.

Expose through Command Scrolls:

- [x] `pkg:list`
- [x] `pkg:info`
- [x] `pkg:install`
- [x] `pkg:remove`
- [x] `pkg:update`

Each command should use the existing Schema + Capability + Command Scroll execution path.

## 9. Contracts & Serialization

These are not the old pre-graph TODOs; only pursue them where the current implementation or a concrete vertical slice requires them.

- [ ] Formalize Scroll identity as a value object where the current code does not already provide the needed boundary.
- [ ] Strengthen Envelope/Scroll serialization contracts.
- [ ] Keep codecs replaceable: NEON, `.ctx`, JSON/YAML, and future formats converge on the canonical resource model.
- [x] Keep metadata discovery/indexing separate from Scroll hydration and execution.
- [ ] Remove genuinely deprecated pre-graph Codice/store/per-type registry structures if any remain in the active implementation.
- [ ] Add signed/traceable resource provenance only when it belongs to the proven Codejitsu boundary; cryptographic provenance is post-MVP unless required earlier.

## 10. Documentation / Context Integrity

- [x] Keep `.context/current-state.ctx` synchronized with the verified repository baseline.
- [x] Keep `.context/roadmap/current.ctx` synchronized with implemented vs planned work.
- [x] Update architecture docs for the lazy index and package boundaries.
- [x] Maintain the ADR documenting the MVP package workspace/monorepo boundary.
- [ ] Update glossary only with terminology that has become a stable Codejitsu concept.
- [ ] Treat `.context/` as architectural/project memory, not as a substitute for tests or code.

## 11. MVP Verification

Before declaring Codejitsu MVP complete:

- [x] Clean Composer install succeeds without OpenSwoole.
- [x] Workspace manifests and active autoload paths validate strictly.
- [x] Scroll discovery/index/source-aware resolution/references work through `ScrollCodex`.
- [x] Metadata queries require zero candidate hydration.
- [x] Command Scrolls drive the CLI end-to-end.
- [x] Namespace help/listing comes from discovered command metadata.
- [x] Current `pkg:*` commands execute through the Command Scroll path.
- [x] Full default PHPUnit suite is green.
- [x] CLI smoke test is green.
- [ ] `.context/` clearly distinguishes implemented Codejitsu behavior from future Shinobi/Sensei/Vessel/Spark work.
- [ ] A clean Codejitsu checkout can serve as the dependency foundation for `shinobiphp/shinobi`.

## Explicitly Post-MVP

Do **not** block Codejitsu MVP on:

- Spark/agent abstractions
- Vessel implementation
- Sensei TUI or code-generation workflows
- model/provider integrations
- OpenSwoole long-running runtime
- async event/outbox/retry/compensation infrastructure
- distributed/service-node resolution
- MCP integration
- ArchIQ integration
- semantic/vector search
- cryptographically signed resource provenance

These belong to the later Shinobi/agentic roadmap unless a concrete Codejitsu requirement moves one back into scope.
